# MSILStackCheck (ImplementationPlan.md M3.b, recon passes-frame.md 8.3) is
# always on and turns every violation of the CIL evaluation-stack rules into an
# internal error, 'MSIL stack check failed in '<function>': <why>: <MI>',
# instead of IL that the JIT rejects with InvalidProgramException or, after a
# bad join, hangs on (plan section 9). Its model: the stack is empty at every
# block entry; each explicit register use pops, each explicit register def
# pushes; KILL, IMPLICIT_DEF, debug and position instructions print nothing and
# are skipped. All seven failure modes are checked here. The pass checks each
# instruction in this order and reports the first failure:
#   multi-push.mir      an instruction pushes more than one value (a call with
#                       two results; CanLowerReturn allows at most one);
#   underflow.mir       an instruction pops more than the stack holds;
#   order.mir           the values on top of the stack are not the
#                       instruction's register operands in operand order;
#   ret-*.mir           'ret' with a depth other than the number of results:
#                       extra values (ret-extra.mir: a value from a void
#                       function; ret-two.mir: two values for one result) or
#                       too few (ret-missing.mir: no value for one result);
#   ret-ops.mir         'ret' at the right depth whose operands do not match
#                       the method's results (one value on the stack, none
#                       named by the RETURN);
#   localloc-depth.mir  'localloc' with something beneath its size.
# After the last instruction of each block it checks
#   block-end.mir       a value left on the stack at the end of a block.
# These are internal errors (report fatal), so the tests use 'not --crash'
# (plan section 2).
#
# Stackified-register state is not serialized in MIR, so every case runs
# MSILExplicitLocals first, which makes each register operand a stack slot.
# ExplicitLocals keeps each ordinary instruction balanced by itself, so the
# underflow, order, ret-ops, localloc and block-end cases use a KILL, which is
# what ExpandPostRAPseudos makes of a COPY whose result is dead: ExplicitLocals
# still materializes a KILL's register operands (it reads a use before it and
# stores a def after it), while MSILStackCheck skips the KILL itself, so the
# pushes and pops of those operands no longer pair up. balanced.mir runs the
# same chain on well-formed input and must not fail.

# RUN: split-file %s %t
# DEFINE: %{check} = -run-pass=msil-explicit-locals,msil-stack-check -o /dev/null

# RUN: not --crash llc -mtriple=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-msil %{check} %t/multi-push.mir 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PUSH
# RUN: not --crash llc -mtriple=x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-msil %{check} %t/multi-push.mir 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PUSH
# PUSH: LLVM ERROR: MSIL stack check failed in 'multi_push': instruction pushes more than one value: {{.*}}CALL &msil_pair

# RUN: not --crash llc -mtriple=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-msil %{check} %t/underflow.mir 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=UNDER
# RUN: not --crash llc -mtriple=x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-msil %{check} %t/underflow.mir 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=UNDER
# UNDER: LLVM ERROR: MSIL stack check failed in 'underflow': evaluation stack underflow: {{.*}}LOCAL_SET_I32 0,

# RUN: not --crash llc -mtriple=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-msil %{check} %t/order.mir 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ORDER
# RUN: not --crash llc -mtriple=x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-msil %{check} %t/order.mir 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ORDER
# ORDER: LLVM ERROR: MSIL stack check failed in 'order': operands are not on top of the evaluation stack in operand order: {{.*}}LOCAL_SET_I32 0,

# RUN: not --crash llc -mtriple=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-msil %{check} %t/ret-extra.mir 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RET-EXTRA
# RUN: not --crash llc -mtriple=x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-msil %{check} %t/ret-extra.mir 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RET-EXTRA
# RET-EXTRA: LLVM ERROR: MSIL stack check failed in 'ret_extra': 'ret' with extra values on the evaluation stack: {{.*}}RETURN

# RUN: not --crash llc -mtriple=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-msil %{check} %t/ret-missing.mir 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RET-MISSING
